\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces (a) Regeneratively cooled engine designed by LEAP~71; the frost on its surface is caused by the cryogenic propellant in the cooling passages (image: LEAP~71~\cite  {LEAP71}). (b) Schematic of regenerative cooling at supercritical pressure through rectangular channels in the chamber wall; near the heated wall the coolant crosses $T_{pb}$ and becomes gas-like, which can trigger heat-transfer deterioration~\cite  {Pizzarelli2018,Nasuti2021,Urbano2013}. (c) Thermophysical properties of CO$_2$ at 8~MPa across the pseudo-boiling temperature $T_{pb}=307.8$~K, normalized by their values at $T_{pb}$ (computed with CoolProp~\cite  {CoolProp2014}).\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:regen}{{1}{4}{(a) Regeneratively cooled engine designed by LEAP~71; the frost on its surface is caused by the cryogenic propellant in the cooling passages (image: LEAP~71~\cite {LEAP71}). (b) Schematic of regenerative cooling at supercritical pressure through rectangular channels in the chamber wall; near the heated wall the coolant crosses $T_{pb}$ and becomes gas-like, which can trigger heat-transfer deterioration~\cite {Pizzarelli2018,Nasuti2021,Urbano2013}. (c) Thermophysical properties of CO$_2$ at 8~MPa across the pseudo-boiling temperature $T_{pb}=307.8$~K, normalized by their values at $T_{pb}$ (computed with CoolProp~\cite {CoolProp2014}).\relax }{figure.caption.1}{}}
