\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces (a) Coolant channels in a mid-scale Haynes~230 nozzle liner at NASA, with the cross-section of one channel (inset)~\cite  {Gradl2019}. (b) DNS of turbulent supercritical CO$_2$ flow in a square duct at 1.5 times the critical pressure, with walls hotter than $T_{pb}$ ($Re_b=12\,000$, $Re_\tau \approx 300$, ongoing work). It shows instantaneous streamwise velocity on planes at $y^+\approx 15$ from the walls and on the cross-section; the outlined quadrant shows the mean streamwise velocity and the streamlines of the secondary flow.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:duct}{{2}{5}{(a) Coolant channels in a mid-scale Haynes~230 nozzle liner at NASA, with the cross-section of one channel (inset)~\cite {Gradl2019}. (b) DNS of turbulent supercritical CO$_2$ flow in a square duct at 1.5 times the critical pressure, with walls hotter than $T_{pb}$ ($Re_b=12\,000$, $Re_\tau \approx 300$, ongoing work). It shows instantaneous streamwise velocity on planes at $y^+\approx 15$ from the walls and on the cross-section; the outlined quadrant shows the mean streamwise velocity and the streamlines of the secondary flow.\relax }{figure.caption.2}{}}
